sd: a shape a command makes at once hands back the select tool

Under the kit, .uno:BasicShapes (and the other custom shape and
polygon commands) with CreateDirectly makes its default object at
once, but the construction tool stays current: FuPermanent switches
back to SID_OBJECT_SELECT only for the rectangle, ellipse, line and
connector slots (bRectangle). The client's next click therefore goes
to FuConstructCustomShape, which draws another default shape where
it lands and selects it instead of the object clicked. Every order
showed it: insert alone, insert then move, insert twice, insert then
select another object (Ely R20.37). Patch 0111's synchronous switch
never ran on this path.

Custom shapes and polygons made directly now switch back like the
rectangles do, through the same call (synchronous under the kit).

diff --git a/sd/source/ui/view/drviewse.cxx b/sd/source/ui/view/drviewse.cxx
